  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Let's write the brute force idea, only to understand its cost.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 4360,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 131,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "First, we generate all permutations of nums, because duplicate values can create duplicate permutations.",
      "start_ms": 5120,
      "end_ms": 12980,
      "start_frame": 154,
      "end_frame": 389,
      "word_count": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "We keep only unique arrangements.",
      "start_ms": 13540,
      "end_ms": 15660,
      "start_frame": 406,
      "end_frame": 470,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Then, we sort those permutations lexicographically.",
      "start_ms": 16400,
      "end_ms": 20680,
      "start_frame": 492,
      "end_frame": 620,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "Now we convert our current array into the same comparable form, and find its position.",
      "start_ms": 21260,
      "end_ms": 28180,
      "start_frame": 638,
      "end_frame": 845,
      "word_count": 15
    },
    {
      "text": "The next position is simply current index plus one.",
      "start_ms": 28700,
      "end_ms": 33060,
      "start_frame": 861,
      "end_frame": 992,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "And to handle the last permutation, we take that position modulo the total number of permutations.",
      "start_ms": 33760,
      "end_ms": 41220,
      "start_frame": 1013,
      "end_frame": 1237,
      "word_count": 16
    },
    {
      "text": "Finally, we copy the selected permutation back into the original array.",
      "start_ms": 41900,
      "end_ms": 47360,
      "start_frame": 1257,
      "end_frame": 1421,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "The code matches the idea exactly.",
      "start_ms": 47820,
      "end_ms": 50340,
      "start_frame": 1435,
      "end_frame": 1510,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "Generate all possibilities, sort them, search for the current one, and select the next.",
      "start_ms": 50940,
      "end_ms": 57440,
      "start_frame": 1528,
      "end_frame": 1723,
      "word_count": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "For tiny inputs, this is fine for understanding.",
      "start_ms": 58120,
      "end_ms": 62380,
      "start_frame": 1744,
      "end_frame": 1871,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "But as a real solution, this approach becomes expensive very quickly.",
      "start_ms": 63040,
      "end_ms": 68520,
      "start_frame": 1891,
      "end_frame": 2056,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "Now let's see why.",
      "start_ms": 69420,
      "end_ms": 70460,
      "start_frame": 2083,
      "end_frame": 2114,
      "word_count": 4
    }
